      {
        "id": 265752,
        "name": "Chief Lackey Rich",
        "username": "Chief_Lackey_Rich",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/6de8d8/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2026-07-01T16:23:43.883Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I don’t think I read the whole thing (there was a fair bit beyond the original Horde storyline, apparently) but I remember the early stages of it.  Like I said, not my favorite even among primarily-scifi comics, but okay and an interesting setting for a short RPG campaign.  Preferred other things in that era like Dynamo Joe, Starslayer, Camelot 3000, Adam Warren’s Dirty Pair books, Grimjack, etc.</p>\n<p>Not sure how well the “everyone uses Experiment for Power Source” thing’s going to work out without further mods, but maybe it’ll be okay.</p>\n<p>I do like the fact it’s Session Zero and the GM has already rolled d12 for each PC to determine how many months they’ve got till the Morituri Process kills them though.  Nice commitment to the premise that you could probably only get away with in an actual play.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2026-07-02T00:59:48.311Z",
