      {
        "id": 265760,
        "name": "Chief Lackey Rich",
        "username": "Chief_Lackey_Rich",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/6de8d8/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2026-07-03T21:43:58.511Z",
        "cooked": "<p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=epKTwxDAtqM\">First actual play session is up already.</a></p>\n<p>Like I suspected, having an entire team where everyone could take the very strong ally-defense/minion Redirect reaction presents some issues, and similarly group access to Unflagging makes penalties quite a bit weaker than the norm.  At least not everyone took either ability, but there’s at least two copies of each.  Universal Experimentation as a power source is thematic as it gets for this campaign, but there just aren’t enough options to avoid significant overlap in ability choices - at least not by the book.  Adding another 2-3 Yellow and 1-2 Green abilities would probably alleviate a lot of that.</p>",
