        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/fjur/{size}/4849_2.png",
        "created_at": "2026-07-05T18:13:33.569Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Te salutamus?</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Chief_Lackey_Rich\" data-post=\"3\" data-topic=\"32395\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/6de8d8/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Chief_Lackey_Rich:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Not sure how well the “everyone uses Experiment for Power Source” thing’s going to work out without further mods, but maybe it’ll be okay.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Looking up the original series, it looks like the Morituri Process had a genetic aspect to it, so to provide more variety perhaps one could mix the Experimentation and Genetic power sources, and allow each hero to select their powers and abilities from either in any combination.</p>",
